$$ 10 \text{ dogs} \times 0.5 \text{ hours/dog/day} = 5 \text{ hours/day} $$

Since we're asked how many hours per week this amounts to, and assuming a week has 7 days, we multiply the daily time by 7:

$$ 5 \text{ hours/day} \times 7 \text{ days/week} = 35 \text{ hours/week} $$

Therefore, the total time Jon spends taking care of the dogs in a week is \boxed{35} hours.

